guard:wasm label_response input JSON (291331 bytes): {"capabilities":{},"tool_args":{"order":"desc","perPage":30,"query":"repo:apache/cloudstack is:open is:issue","sort":"created"},"tool_name":"search_issues","tool_result":{"content":[{"text":"{\"total_count\":650,\"incomplete_results\":false,\"items\":[{\"id\":5612465324,\"number\":14251,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"CKS Deployed with external ETCD is not secure\",\"body\":\"### problem\\n\\nWhen CKS provisions a Kubernetes cluster with external etcd, the generated\\nkubeadm configuration points the API server at etcd over plaintext HTTP with\\nno client-certificate authentication. The etcd client/peer endpoints are\\nserved as `http://` and the kubeadm `external` etcd block has empty\\n`caFile`, `certFile`, and `keyFile` values:\\n\\n    etcd:\\n      external:\\n        caFile: \\\"\\\"\\n        certFile: \\\"\\\"\\n        keyFile: \\\"\\\"\\n        endpoints:\\n        - http://10.x.x.x:2379\\n        - http://10.x.x.x:2379\\n        - http://10.x.x.x:2379\\n        httpEndpoints:\\n        - http://10.x.x.x:2379\\n        - http://10.x.x.x:2379\\n        - http://10.x.x.x:2379\\n\\nBecause etcd is the Kubernetes API server's unconditionally-trusted source of\\ntruth, any workload that can reach TCP 2379 can read and write cluster state\\nwithout authentication and over an unencrypted channel. This is effectively a\\nfull-cluster-compromise primitive: unauthenticated read of all Secrets and\\nunauthenticated write of arbitrary objects.\\nAs per Kubernetes Documentation here: https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/administer-cluster/configure-upgrade-etcd/#securing-etcd-clusters\\n\\n### versions\\n\\nCKS (CloudStack Kubernetes Service) — external etcd configuration \\n\\n### The steps to reproduce the bug\\n\\n# 1. Reachability to the etcd client port\\nnc -vz 10.x.x.x 2379\\n\\n# 2. etcd answers over cleartext HTTP (no TLS)\\ncurl -v http://10.x.x.x:2379/health\\n# -\\u003e {\\\"health\\\":\\\"true\\\"} over plain HTTP\\n\\n# 3. No client certificate required\\nETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl \\\\\\n  --endpoints=http://10.x.x.x:2379,http://10.x.x.x:2379,http://10.x.x.x:2379 \\\\\\n  endpoint status --write-out=table\\nETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --endpoints=http://10.x.x.x:2379 member list --write-out=table\\n\\n# 4. Write access, proven non-destructively under a namespace k8s does not use,\\n#    then cleaned up (does NOT touch the /registry/ prefix):\\nETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --endpoints=http://10.x.x.x:2379 \\\\\\n  put /pentest/poc \\\"unauthenticated write proof\\\"\\nETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --endpoints=http://10.x.x.x:2379 get --prefix /pentest/\\nETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --endpoints=http://10.x.x.x:2379 del --prefix /pentest/\\n\\n# 5. Cleartext confirmation on the wire\\ntcpdump -i any -A -c 40 host 10.x.x.x and port 2379\\n\\n### What to do about it?\\n\\n**1. Immediate fix — mutual TLS on external etcd (this issue)**\\n\\nCKS should provision external etcd with TLS and client-certificate\\nauthentication, and populate the kubeadm `external` block with real key\\nmaterial instead of empty strings:\\n\\n    etcd:\\n      external:\\n        caFile: /etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt\\n        certFile: /etc/kubernetes/pki/apiserver-etcd-client.crt\\n        keyFile: /etc/kubernetes/pki/apiserver-etcd-client.key\\n        endpoints:\\n        - https://10.x.x.x:2379\\n        - https://10.x.x.x:2379\\n        - https://10.x.x.x:2379\\n\\n**2. Follow-up — automated certificate rotation (separate PR / issue)**\\n\\nIntroducing etcd mTLS adds certificates that expire, so the fix is only durable\\nif renewal is automated. Without it, clusters will silently drift toward an\\noutage when the etcd CA or the `apiserver-etcd-client` certificate lapses, and\\noperators may be tempted to revert to HTTP to \\\"make it work again\\\" — which would\\nreintroduce this exact vulnerability.\\n\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mw-0\",\"id\":26769729,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzY5NzI5\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26769729?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/mw-0\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mw-0\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mw-0/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mw-0/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mw-0/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mw-0/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mw-0/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mw-0/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mw-0/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mw-0/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mw-0/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":11243221368,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/bug\",\"name\":\"bug\",\"color\":\"ededed\",\"default\":true,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAACniXxeA\"}],\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-28T09:36:49Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-28T09:36:49Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14251\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/14251\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14251/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14251/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14251/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14251/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABTodsrA\"},{\"id\":5602620972,\"number\":14250,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"[repo-status] CloudStack Weekly Status — 20–27 September 2026\",\"body\":\"## Weekly status: 20–27 September 2026 🌟\\n\\nCloudStack continues to make strong infrastructure progress this week, with a significant storage and migration capability merged into `main`.\\n\\n### Highlights\\n\\n- **VMware-to-KVM migration expanded:** commit [0a5bf30a](https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/commit/0a5bf30af32bdea5a209f3f993cbd6a43301d0f9) landed on 24 September, covering cold (VDDK) and warm (CBT) migration into **Ceph/RBD** and **Linstor**.\\n- **Import workflow improved:** `importVm` now adopts existing RBD root volumes and Linstor root/data volumes, reducing friction for migrations and existing-storage adoption.\\n- **Repository health:** the local `main` checkout is clean and aligned with `origin/main`.\\n\\n### Progress toward project goals\\n\\nThis work advances CloudStack’s interoperability and migration goals while broadening practical options for operators moving workloads from VMware to open storage backends. It also strengthens the path for incremental modernization without requiring every workload to be rebuilt from scratch.\\n\\n### Recommendations and next steps\\n\\n1. Exercise the cold and warm migration paths across representative Ceph/RBD and Linstor topologies, including failure and rollback scenarios.\\n2. Refresh migration and `importVm` documentation with prerequisites, supported combinations, and operator examples.\\n3. Track early adopter feedback and prioritize follow-up fixes for edge cases in volume adoption, networking, and post-migration validation.\\n4. Keep review and integration momentum high on related storage, hypervisor, and upgrade work.\\n\\n\\u003e Note: the GitHub issue/PR activity feed timed out during collection, so this report intentionally highlights only activity directly verified from the repository commit history and successfully retrieved metadata.\\n\\nThanks to everyone contributing to another productive week of CloudStack development! 🚀\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\u003e Generated by [Weekly Repo Status](https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/actions/runs/36318807044) · gpt56 196.9K · [◷](https://github.com/search?q=repo%3Aapache%2Fcloudstack+is%3Aissue+%22gh-aw-workflow-call-id%3A+apache%2Fcloudstack%2Fweekly-repo-status%22\\u0026type=issues)\\n\\u003e\\n\\u003cdetails\\u003e\\n\\u003csummary\\u003eAdd this agentic workflows to your repo\\u003c/summary\\u003e\\n\\nTo install this agentic workflow, run\\n\\n```\\ngh aw add githubnext/agentics/workflows/repo-status.md@main\\n```\\n\\u003c/details\\u003e\\n\\n\\n\\u003c!-- gh-aw-agentic-workflow: Weekly Repo Status, engine: copilot, version: 1.0.52, model: gpt-5.6-luna, id: 36318807044, workflow_id: weekly-repo-status, run: https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/actions/runs/36318807044 --\\u003e\\n\\n\\u003c!-- gh-aw-workflow-id: weekly-repo-status --\\u003e\\n\\u003c!-- gh-aw-workflow-call-id: apache/cloudstack/weekly-repo-status --\\u003e\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"github-actions[bot]\",\"id\":41898282,\"node_id\":\"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apps/github-actions\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"Bot\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":11108839396,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/report\",\"name\":\"report\",\"color\":\"ededed\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAACliNv5A\"},{\"id\":11849802122,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/weekly-status\",\"name\":\"weekly-status\",\"color\":\"ededed\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAACwk2hig\"}],\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-27T12:27:57Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-27T12:27:57Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14250\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/14250\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14250/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14250/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14250/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14250/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABTfE2LA\"},{\"id\":5582821606,\"number\":14248,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"listPublicIpAddresses NullPointerException on shared networks with a VR (4.22)\",\"body\":\"### problem\\n\\nOn 4.22.1.0, listPublicIpAddresses with forvirtualnetwork=false sometimes fails with a 530:\\n\\n\\n```\\n2026-09-25 06:50:01,162 ERROR [c.c.a.ApiServer] (qtp2038105753-72330:[ctx-762cfe49, ctx-ac3b837a, ctx-e861c603]) (logid:e972f310) unhandled exception executing api command: [Ljava.lang.String;@4e95c7d5 java.lang.NullPointerException: Cannot invoke \\\"java.lang.Long.longValue()\\\" because \\\"this.instanceId\\\" is null\\n2026-09-25 06:50:01,165 INFO  [a.c.c.a.ApiServlet] (qtp2038105753-72330:[ctx-762cfe49, ctx-ac3b837a, ctx-e861c603]) (logid:e972f310) (userId=8 accountId=2 sessionId=null) 0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1 -- GET allocatedonly=false\\u0026apikey=\\u003credacted\\u003e\\u0026command=listPublicIpAddresses\\u0026forvirtualnetwork=false\\u0026listall=true\\u0026page=1\\u0026pagesize=500\\u0026response=json\\u0026signature=\\u003credacted\\u003e 530 Cannot invoke \\\"java.lang.Long.longValue()\\\" because \\\"this.instanceId\\\" is null\\n```\\nThe same request succeeds on some attempts and fails on others.\\n\\nIt looks like the DomainRouter branch added to ApiResponseHelper.showVmInfoForSharedNetworks() in #10458 is hitting the VR's placeholder NIC, which has a null instance_id. Our shared network has two NIC rows for the VR's IP (the placeholder and the real one), and the NIC lookup can return either, which would explain why it's intermittent. It seems to be the same or a similar problem as #8622, which #8624 fixed for the system VM branch.\\n\\n### versions\\n\\nACS 4.22.1.0, KVM, advanced zone. The shared network offering uses VirtualRouter for DHCP, DNS and UserData.\\n\\n### The steps to reproduce the bug\\n\\n1. Create a shared network whose offering uses VirtualRouter for DHCP/DNS, and deploy a VM on it so the VR starts.\\n2. As admin, call listPublicIpAddresses networkid=\\u003cnetwork\\u003e forvirtualnetwork=false a few times.\\n3. Some calls fail with the NPE above.\\n\\n### What to do about it?\\n\\nfindNonPlaceHolderByIp4AddressAndNetworkId() looks to skip placeholder IP addresses, so should be able to change this line in ApiResponseHelper.java:\\n\\nChange:\\n```\\n        if (!forVirtualNetworks) {\\n            NicVO nic = ApiDBUtils.findByIp4AddressAndNetworkId(ipAddr.getAddress().toString(), ipAddr.getNetworkId());\\n```\\n\\nTo:\\n```\\n        if (!forVirtualNetworks) {\\n            NicVO nic = ApiDBUtils.findNonPlaceHolderByIp4AddressAndNetworkId(ipAddr.getAddress().toString(), ipAddr.getNetworkId());\\n```\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"MitchDrage\",\"id\":25337396,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjI1MzM3Mzk2\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/25337396?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/MitchDrage\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/MitchDrage\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/MitchDrage/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/MitchDrage/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/MitchDrage/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/MitchDrage/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/MitchDrage/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/MitchDrage/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/MitchDrage/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/MitchDrage/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/MitchDrage/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":11243221368,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/bug\",\"name\":\"bug\",\"color\":\"ededed\",\"default\":true,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAACniXxeA\"}],\"comments\":0,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-25T12:32:33Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-25T12:32:33Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14248\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/14248\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14248/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14248/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14248/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14248/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABTMMY5g\"},{\"id\":5571337921,\"number\":14244,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"CKS: upgradeKubernetesCluster fails on control node when binaries ISO ships headlamp.yaml instead of dashboard.yaml\",\"body\":\"### problem\\n\\nSince 4.23, create-kubernetes-binaries-iso.sh packages the Headlamp dashboard as headlamp.yaml\\ninstead of dashboard.yaml. The cluster create path (k8s-control-node.yml) handles both files,\\nbut upgrade-kubernetes.sh still hardcodes:\\n\\n    /opt/bin/kubectl apply -f ${BINARIES_DIR}/dashboard.yaml\\n\\nThe script runs with bash -e, so on the first control node it exits non-zero after kubeadm\\nupgrade apply and the kubelet swap have already succeeded. The worker retries\\n(cloud.kubernetes.cluster.upgrade.retries) and then fails the job, leaving the control node\\non the new version but cordoned, the workers on the old version, the cluster in Alert,\\nand the DB still recording the old version.\\n\\nManagement server log:\\n  SSH execution of command sudo ./upgrade-kubernetes.sh\\u003crand\\u003e.sh 1.36.0 true false false true\\n  has an error status code in return. Result output: Installing binaries from /mnt/k8sdisk/\\n  Failed to upgrade Kubernetes cluster : single, unable to upgrade Kubernetes node on VM : single-control-...\\n\\nRunning the script by hand on the control node shows:\\n  error: the path \\\"/mnt/k8sdisk//dashboard.yaml\\\" does not exist\\n\\nISO contents:\\n  10-kubeadm.conf autoscaler.yaml cni cri-tools docker headlamp.yaml k8s kubelet.service\\n  manifest.yaml network.yaml provider.yaml snapshot-crds.yaml\\n\\n### versions\\n\\nACS 4.23.0.0 (also present on main at 0a5bf30)\\nKubernetes upgrade 1.35.8 -\\u003e 1.36.0, ISO built with the 4.23 create-kubernetes-binaries-iso.sh\\nHypervisor: kvm Network: isolated..\\n\\n### The steps to reproduce the bug\\n\\n1. Build and register a Kubernetes version ISO with the 4.23 create-kubernetes-binaries-iso.sh (contains headlamp.yaml)\\n2. Deploy a CKS cluster on the previous minor version\\n3. Call upgradeKubernetesCluster to the new version\\n4. Job fails on the first control node; kubectl get nodes shows control on new version, SchedulingDisabled\\n\\n### What to do about it?\\n\\nMake upgrade-kubernetes.sh use the same fallback as k8s-control-node.yml: apply headlamp.yaml\\nif present, else dashboard.yaml, else warn. I'll open a PR. Workaround: patch\\nscript/upgrade-kubernetes.sh inside the management server jar and restart.\\nI already have tested a fix and will put in a PR.\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"mw-0\",\"id\":26769729,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjI2NzY5NzI5\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26769729?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/mw-0\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mw-0\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mw-0/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mw-0/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mw-0/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mw-0/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mw-0/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mw-0/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mw-0/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mw-0/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/mw-0/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":11243221368,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/bug\",\"name\":\"bug\",\"color\":\"ededed\",\"default\":true,\"node_id\":\"LA_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAACniXxeA\"}],\"comments\":1,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-24T16:23:46Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-24T16:23:50Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14244\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/14244\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14244/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14244/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14244/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14244/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABTBPewQ\"},{\"id\":5570090892,\"number\":14242,\"state\":\"open\",\"state_reason\":\"reopened\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"Automatic HTTP retries and 50-second timeouts\",\"body\":\"Hi Team,\\n\\nWe are observing an issue where long-running HTTP POST requests taking over 50 seconds are being terminated with an HTTP 499 status code and automatically retried every 50 seconds with the identical x_request_id.\\n\\nOur analysis shows that the 50-second timeout and retry loop are being triggered by the CloudStack Virtual Router's default HAProxy configuration (timeout server 50s and retries 3) on the Load Balancer service.\\n\\n\\n\\n**kv-dev logs --tail 100 -f  nginx-666b6675d8-m7qpt|grep \\\"POST /v2/cr\\\"\\n10.1.1.1 - - [24/Sep/2026:12:09:27 +0000] \\\"POST /v2/cr/tenants/b8d1dc4d-5961-4ff9-9eeb-a36d2f73f1bb/call_reports HTTP/1.1\\\" 499 0 \\\"https://vvstei.com/app/reports/callReports\\\" \\\"Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 15; Pixel 9) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/150.0.0.0 Mobile Safari/537.36\\\" x_forwarded_for=\\\"-\\\" x_request_id=\\\"534d2a13-15b6-46c0-ad9c-291f73c55053\\\" request_time=\\\"50.002\\\" upstream_addr=\\\"10.105.79.92:9080\\\" upstream_status=\\\"-\\\" upstream_response_time=\\\"50.002\\\"real_ip=\\\"-\\\" \\n10.1.1.1 - - [24/Sep/2026:12:10:17 +0000] \\\"POST /v2/cr/tenants/b8d1dc4d-5961-4ff9-9eeb-a36d2f73f1bb/call_reports HTTP/1.1\\\" 499 0 \\\"https://vvstei.comreports/callReports\\\" \\\"Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 15; Pixel 9) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/150.0.0.0 Mobile Safari/537.36\\\" x_forwarded_for=\\\"-\\\" x_request_id=\\\"534d2a13-15b6-46c0-ad9c-291f73c55053\\\" request_time=\\\"50.001\\\" upstream_addr=\\\"10.105.79.92:9080\\\" upstream_status=\\\"-\\\" upstream_response_time=\\\"50.001\\\"real_ip=\\\"-\\\" \\n10.1.1.1 - - [24/Sep/2026:12:11:07 +0000] \\\"POST /v2/cr/tenants/b8d1dc4d-5961-4ff9-9eeb-a36d2f73f1bb/call_reports HTTP/1.1\\\" 499 0 \\\"https://vvstei.com/reports/callReports\\\" \\\"Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 15; Pixel 9) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/150.0.0.0 Mobile Safari/537.36\\\" x_forwarded_for=\\\"-\\\" x_request_id=\\\"534d2a13-15b6-46c0-ad9c-291f73c55053\\\" request_time=\\\"50.003\\\" upstream_addr=\\\"10.105.79.92:9080\\\" upstream_status=\\\"-\\\" upstream_response_time=\\\"50.001\\\"real_ip=\\\"-\\\"** \\n\\n\\n\\nCould you please assist us with one of the following solutions?\\n\\nUpdate HAProxy settings on the Virtual Router:\\n\\nIncrease timeout server and timeout client to 900s (15 minutes).\\n\\nSet retries to 0.\\n\\nAlternatively:\\n\\nProvide guidance or update the CloudStack global parameters (haproxy.timeout.server) for the Virtual Router offering.\\n\\nPlease let us know if you need any additional logs or details.\\n\\nThanks,\",\"author_association\":\"NONE\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"vishnuvs369\",\"id\":54799446,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjU0Nzk5NDQ2\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54799446?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/vishnuvs369\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/vishnuvs369\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/vishnuvs369/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/vishnuvs369/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/vishnuvs369/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/vishnuvs369/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/vishnuvs369/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/vishnuvs369/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/vishnuvs369/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/vishnuvs369/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/vishnuvs369/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":37843366,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/type:enhancement\",\"name\":\"type:enhancement\",\"color\":\"84b6eb\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzg0MzM2Ng==\"},{\"id\":584073391,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:virtual-router\",\"name\":\"component:virtual-router\",\"color\":\"ffaaeb\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWw1ODQwNzMzOTE=\"},{\"id\":592559219,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/labels/component:networking\",\"name\":\"component:networking\",\"color\":\"f9d0c4\",\"description\":\"\",\"default\":false,\"node_id\":\"MDU6TGFiZWw1OTI1NTkyMTk=\"}],\"comments\":2,\"created_at\":\"2026-09-24T14:44:28Z\",\"updated_at\":\"2026-09-28T13:03:09Z\",\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14242\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/apache/cloudstack/issues/14242\",\"comments_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14242/comments\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14242/events\",\"labels_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14242/labels{/name}\",\"repository_url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack\",\"reactions\":{\"total_count\":0,\"+1\":0,\"-1\":0,\"laugh\":0,\"confused\":0,\"heart\":0,\"hooray\":0,\"rocket\":0,\"eyes\":0,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/apache/cloudstack/issues/14242/reactions\"},\"node_id\":\"I_kwDOAJTq2M8AAAABTADXjA\"},{\"id\":5567637365,\"number\":14241,\"state\":\"open\",\"locked\":false,\"title\":\"[JAVA] Move to JDK21\",\"body\":\"### The required feature described as a wish\\n\\nCloudStack now runs on JDK 17, strict requirement.\\n\\nJDK 17 is EoL this September (Oracle) and in less than a 1y with other \\\"providers\\\":\\n\\nVendor Support End Dates for OpenJDK 17\\n- Oracle JDK 17: Premier Support ends on September 30, 2026 (with Extended Support running through September 30, 2029).\\n- Microsoft Build of OpenJDK 17: Supported until September 30, 2027.\\n- Eclipse Temurin (Adoptium): Supported until at least October 31, 2027.\\n- Red Hat build of OpenJDK 17: Supported until December 31, 2027.\\n\\nJDK25 is too cutting-edge and has a narrow ecosystem, so the recommended LTS to switch to is  JDK 21.\",\"author_association\":\"CONTRIBUTOR\",\"user\":{\"login\":\"andrijapanicsb\",\"id\":45762285,\"node_id\":\"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1NzYyMjg1\",\"avatar_url\":\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45762285?v=4\",\"html_url\":\"https://github.com/andrijapanicsb\",\"gravatar_id\":\"\",\"type\":\"User\",\"site_admin\":false,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb\",\"events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/events{/privacy}\",\"following_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/following{/other_user}\",\"followers_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/followers\",\"gists_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/gists{/gist_id}\",\"organizations_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/orgs\",\"received_events_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/received_events\",\"repos_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/repos\",\"starred_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/starred{/owner}{/repo}\",\"subscriptions_url\":\"https://api.github.com/users/andrijapanicsb/subscriptions\"},\"labels\":[{\"id\":4008138977,\"url\":\"https://api.github.com/repos/a